course: dictionary
lesson: 6003
title: Mecca: a holy city and a favourite place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mecca, also spelled Makkah, is the holiest city of Islam, in Saudi Arabia. It is where the Prophet Muhammad was born, and it is the place Muslims travel to on the hajj, a pilgrimage.
explain: Muslims everywhere face towards Mecca when they pray, so Mecca is at the centre of their prayers. In a mosque people pray side by side in rows facing Mecca, led by an imam.
explain: With a small m, mecca is a word for any place that many people with the same interest love to visit. «Paris is a mecca for artists» means that many artists go there because they love it.
fact: Mecca is the holiest city of Islam, and it is in Saudi Arabia.
fact: The Prophet Muhammad was born in Mecca.
fact: Muslims face towards Mecca when they pray.
fact: A pilgrimage is a journey made for religious reasons; Muslims make the hajj pilgrimage to Mecca.
fact: «Mansa Musa made his pilgrimage to Mecca in 1324» and gave away so much gold that its price fell in Cairo.
exercise: What is Mecca? | *The holiest city of Islam, in Saudi Arabia | A river in Egypt | A famous football stadium in Europe
exercise: When do Muslims face towards Mecca? | When they eat their lunch | When they go swimming | When it is raining | *When they pray
exercise: «Paris is a mecca for artists.» What does mecca mean here? | *A place that many people with the same interest love to visit | A type of boat | A holy book | A painting of a city
test: «The Five Pillars are: the declaration of faith, prayer five times a day, giving to the poor, fasting in Ramadan and the pilgrimage to Mecca.» Which pillar is about a journey to Mecca? | *The pilgrimage to Mecca | Prayer five times a day | Fasting in Ramadan | Giving to the poor
test: Which sentence uses mecca with a small m to mean a favourite place? | *«Our town is a mecca for skateboarders.» | «The mosque faces Mecca.» | «Mecca is in Saudi Arabia.» | «The Prophet Muhammad was born in Mecca.»
exam: Which of these is part of the Five Pillars of Islam? | Learning a new language | *Making the pilgrimage to Mecca (Hajj) | Playing sport every week | Reading a school newspaper
